; What `show` refuses now that the checker resolves it (phase 0 of the
; traits removal), every one under AX3025 so the code a reader already
; looks for still finds it.
;
;   1  a type VARIABLE - a generic function's own `a` - is the refusal
;      it always was, word for word: `Show.ax`'s instances still claim
;      the name, so the trait path reports it before the builtin is
;      asked
;   2  a constructor applied to a type variable - `(Box a)` inside a
;      generic function - is the builtin's own wording of shape 1,
;      because no `(impl (Show Box))` exists to fall back on
;   3  a `data` or `struct` the builtin cannot take apart: `Holder`
;      holds a `Foreign`, and the refusal names the field type and
;      lands at the CALL, before anything is generated
(import IO)

(:: generic (-> a Int))

;@axiom:effect(io)
(fn (generic x)
  {
    (println x)
    0
  }
)

(struct Holder
  (f : Foreign))

(data Box a
  (MkBox a))

(:: boxed (-> (Box a) Int))

;@axiom:effect(io)
(fn (boxed b)
  {
    (println b)
    0
  }
)

(:: main Int)

;@axiom:effect(io)
(fn (main)
  (let ((h 
    (Holder
      (cast Foreign 0)
    )
  ))
    {
      (println h)
      0
    }
  )
)
